      trivia: "Saka's blends carry the distinctive naming culture he established in his Drew Estate years. The “9” of Liga Privada No. 9 marks the ninth blend he devised; Mi Querida means “my mistress”; Muestra de Saka, “Saka's sample”; Sin Compromiso, “without compromise” — each directly reflecting the maker's private story and pride. Above all, sobremesa is an untranslatable Spanish word for the time spent lingering in conversation around the table after a meal, emblematic of Saka's aesthetic of the cigar as an “extension of ease”."
